  "tagline": "Ambitious lock-free embedded Rust database whose 1.0 rewrite has stalled in alpha.",
  "description": "sled is an embedded key-value store for Rust that popularised modern lock-free, log-structured B-tree ideas in the Rust ecosystem, with an API similar to a thread-safe BTreeMap plus transactions, watch subscriptions and merge operators. The stable 0.34.x line dates from 2021, and the author's ground-up 1.0 rewrite has been in alpha since 2024 with only sporadic commits since. The project calls itself beta software and warns of high space usage and an unstable on-disk format. Many Rust projects have moved to redb or Fjall; sled remains interesting as a design reference.",
